26   Payment on a time-and-material basis against proof                   001871
26                                                                        001872
26                                                                        001873
26   Payment on a time-and-material basis against proof                   001874
26                                                                        001875
26   Carrying out hourly-rate work against proof and at the               001876
26   request of the local site management. Work is paid if                001877
26   its execution was ordered in writing by site                         001878
26   management.                                                          001879
26                                                                        001880
26   Only the working hours actually performed for personnel              001881
26   and equipment are charged. If a special PER00037 is                  001882
26   kept for the works, no payment is granted for the                    001883
26   supervisory personnel unless expressly agreed otherwise              001884
26   beforehand.                                                          001885
26                                                                        001886
26   Insofar as hourly charge-out rates claimed are not                   001887
26   contained in the bid, the contractor is obliged, at the              001888
26   client's request, to furnish proof of the actual labour              001889
26   costs on the basis of the payroll lists.                             001890
26                                                                        001891
26   Wages above the collective agreement and ancillary                   001892
26   labour costs are to be proven to the client on request.              001893
26                                                                        001894
26   Surcharges on the charge-out rates for night, Sunday,                001895
26   public holiday and additional work (overtime) ordered                001896
26   by the client or for which the client is responsible                 001897
26   are to be proven separately; they are paid in the                    001898
26   amount of the collective agreement. For night, Sunday                001899
26   and public holiday work, only the contribution to                    001900
26   statutory accident insurance is paid as a surcharge.                 001901
26   For additional work, additionallythe social costs are                001902
26   paid.                                                                001903
26                                                                        001904
26   All surcharges such as overheads, social contributions,              001905
26   lodging allowance, travel allowances etc. are to be                  001906
26   included in the hourly rate. Billing is against proof.               001907
26   The daywork sheets are to be signed daily by the                     001908
26   building owner, as otherwise the hourly-rate work will               001909
26   not be recognised. Billing with the client is to take                001910
26   place promptly.                                                      001911
26                                                                        001912
26   The bid total of the hourly-rate work is included in                 001913
26   the bid evaluation, the hourly-rate work is however not              001914
26   commissioned. The offered [PERSON_126] become part of                001915
26   the contract.                                                        001916
26                                                                        001917
26   The contractor has no claim to the use of the hours                  001918
26   provided for, for more or fewer hours worked the same                001919
26   charge-out rates apply.                                              001920
